    "intro_html":  "Cordon bleu means blue ribbon, and the original dish involves pounding meat flat, rolling it around ham and cheese, breading it, and praying it does not leak in the pan. Nobody is doing that fourteen times. This takes all the same parts, turkey, ham, Swiss, mustard, a buttery crumb top, and lays them into a casserole. Each serving carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Two proteins in one pan for that price is arithmetic worth paying attention to.",
